1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,904
A request arrives to buy forty-five shares of NVDA at a hundred dollars.

2
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:15,815
The portfolio holds twenty thousand nine hundred eighty-three dollars, and its per-trade ceiling is five percent.

3
00:00:15,815 --> 00:00:19,546
The guard approves ten point four nine units, not forty-five.

4
00:00:19,546 --> 00:00:22,482
One thousand forty-nine dollars, eighteen cents.

5
00:00:22,482 --> 00:00:25,112
The model asked; the code decided the size.

6
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:26,947
Four hundred and fifty shares?

7
00:00:26,947 --> 00:00:27,926
No - forty-five.

8
00:00:27,926 --> 00:00:30,250
Either way, the ceiling is what it is.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,802
Three agents argue before that request ever reaches the guard.

10
00:00:33,802 --> 00:00:41,479
A bull analyst builds the case to buy, a risk assessor builds the case to sell, and neither prompt contains the other side's argument.

11
00:00:41,479 --> 00:00:47,151
A chief investment officer weighs both and has to name the strongest objection it could not answer.

12
00:00:47,151 --> 00:00:51,390
Their disagreement is stored as claims and rebuttals, not summarised away.

13
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:53,412
The same guard refuses twice more.

14
00:00:53,412 --> 00:00:59,776
A request after a realised loss of six hundred dollars is blocked, because the daily limit is five hundred.

15
00:00:59,776 --> 00:01:03,582
The loss that already happened is the reason new risk is frozen.

16
00:01:03,582 --> 00:01:06,080
The guard does not know which agent asked.

17
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,210
It knows the limit.

18
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:10,416
Every refusal is recorded with the rule that produced it.

19
00:01:10,416 --> 00:01:17,840
Run the same decision again and you get the same answer, from a replay bundle you can open in a browser with no database and no key.

20
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:20,990
The numbers on screen are the numbers in the transcript.

21
00:01:20,990 --> 00:01:22,440
Open source, on GitHub.

22
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:26,410
Read the transcript, check the arithmetic, then try to beat it.
